[1mNAME[0m[m
       head - output the first part of files[m
[m
[1mSYNOPSIS[0m[m
       [1mhead [22m[[4mOPTION[24m]... [[4mFILE[24m]...[m
[m
[1mDESCRIPTION[0m[m
       Print the first 10 lines of each FILE to standard output.  With more than one FILE, precede each with a header giving the file name.[m
[m
       With no FILE, or when FILE is -, read standard input.[m
[m
       Mandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.[m
[m
       [1m-c[22m, [1m--bytes[22m=[4m[-]NUM[0m[m
              print the first NUM bytes of each file; with the leading '-', print all but the last NUM bytes of each file[m
[m
       [1m-n[22m, [1m--lines[22m=[4m[-]NUM[0m[m
              print the first NUM lines instead of the first 10; with the leading '-', print all but the last NUM lines of each file[m
[m
       [1m-q[22m, [1m--quiet[22m, [1m--silent[0m[m
              never print headers giving file names[m
[m
       [1m-v[22m, [1m--verbose[0m[m
              always print headers giving file names[m
[m
       [1m-z[22m, [1m--zero-terminated[0m[m
              line delimiter is NUL, not newline[m
[m
       [1m--help [22mdisplay this help and exit[m
[m
       [1m--version[0m[m
              output version information and exit[m
[m
       NUM  may  have  a multiplier suffix: b 512, kB 1000, K 1024, MB 1000*1000, M 1024*1024, GB 1000*1000*1000, G 1024*1024*1024, and so on for T, P, E, Z, Y, R, Q.  Binary prefixes can be used, too:[m
       KiB=K, MiB=M, and so on.[m
[m
